-- SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
-- risk: additive
-- (event_type_view_permissions restated whole: same signature, same rows plus
-- one; same ACL. events_type_check and validation_policies_event_type_check
-- each gain one type.)
--
-- #3132 (decided in #3012), slice 3 -- an assistant proposes a change of the
-- workspace's bank account, and the person confirms it in the app, seeing the
-- account as it is now and as it would become.
--
--   write  set_payment_instructions  the Payment methods screen's own write:
--                                    workspaces.payment_instructions
--                                    (manageIntegrations, money on)
--
-- In scope: the bank account only (iban, bic, bank_name, account_number,
-- bank_code, qr_iban). The other ways to pay (PayPal, Wero, Lydia, Wise, the
-- reference line) and every payment-provider key or token stay in the app;
-- a name a credential goes by is refused with secret_in_app_only.
--
-- The app writes the column directly, under workspaces_update and the column
-- guard of 0361, which lets manageIntegrations (and the owner) write it. The
-- operation asks the same permission again for the person, and checks what the
-- app does not: an IBAN and a QR-IBAN by their mod-97 check (the suppliers'
-- supplier_iban_check, 0458), a BIC by its shape, a QR-IBAN by its Swiss
-- institution range, every value by its length.
--
-- The target (mcp_target_set_payment_instructions) names every field that
-- changes, from -> to, over the stored account; its revision is that account,
-- so a proposal made before the account changed is stale, at the answer and
-- again at the repeated call. It refuses, before anyone is asked, an invalid
-- value or a change that changes nothing (22023 -> validation_error).
--
-- After the person confirmed, the operation writes the account and records
-- ONE audit event of the new type payment_instructions_change: actor = the
-- person who confirmed, subject = the workspace's owner, so it reaches the
-- owner's notifications whoever made the change (and everyone holding
-- manageIntegrations reads it through the type's view permission). The event
-- names the fields that changed and the last four characters of the IBAN
-- before and after; the account itself is never written to an event.

